{#
  Rendered from the cache: declarations, one file per distribution. apt fails
  the whole `apt-get update` when a single source is unreachable, so a runner
  must never carry another distribution's entry.

  The source names the real mirror, not the service name, which coredns, the
  container's resolver, cannot resolve; the compose overrides map the
  hostname to the frontend via extra_hosts.

  A distribution that does not install through apt renders an empty file. The
  bind mount is unconditional in the compose overrides, and docker would
  create a host directory here if the source were missing.
#}
{% if CACHE_PACKAGE_APT_SOURCE %}
deb [trusted=yes] {{ CACHE_PACKAGE_APT_SOURCE }} {{ CACHE_PACKAGE_APT_SUITE }} main
{% endif %}
